[?2004l[?2004h> # BILL-212 handoff
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Fixed
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Renewals were always clamped to day 28 and then calculated from the previous
[?2004l[?2004h> renewal, permanently losing month-end and leap-day anchors. Proration also used
[?2004l[?2004h> fixed 30/365-day denominators, credited the old plan at the change-date price,
[?2004l[?2004h> and treated monthly/annual switches as same-interval changes.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> - Clamp to the target month's actual last day and derive every renewal from
[?2004l[?2004h>   the original anchor. Renewal dates start a new half-open cycle.
[?2004l[?2004h> - Use actual cycle days and the old price effective at cycle start.
[?2004l[?2004h> - Round the exact rational once using integer half-even arithmetic, independent
[?2004l[?2004h>   of Decimal precision.
[?2004l[?2004h> - Preserve anchors for same-interval changes; charge the full new price and
[?2004l[?2004h>   re-anchor interval switches. Invoice line periods follow the respective cycles.
[?2004l[?2004h> - Keep the existing public APIs unchanged.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Verification
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Added 13 regression tests, all passing, including subprocess CLI previews for
